l is considered to be under the archerΓÇÖs fire if and only if all points of this cell, including border points are located inside the circle or on its border.\n\nThe picture below shows the borders for shot ranges equal to 3 , 4 and 5 . The archer is depicted as A . \n \nFind the number of cells that are under fire for some archer.\n\n## Input\n\nThe first and only line of input contains a single positive integer k ΓÇö the archer's shot range ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë k ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 6 ).\n\n## Output\n\nPrint the single number, the number of cells that are under fire.\n\nPlease do not use the %lld specificator to read or write 64-bit integers in C++. It is preferred to use the cout stream (also you may use the %I64d specificator).\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n3\n```\n```\n7\n```","type":"text"}],"contestId":78,"index":"D","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Archer's Shot","problemKey":"78-D","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"2 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/78/problem/D"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 8","number":8,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 9","number":9,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 10","number":10,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 11","number":11,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 12","number":12,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 13","number":13,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 14","number":14,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 15","number":15,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 16","number":16,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 17","number":17,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 18","number":18,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 19","number":19,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 20","number":20,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]}],"assets":[],"contentBlocks":[{"sequence":0,"text":"## Problem Statement\n\nThey've screwed something up yet again... In one nuclear reactor of a research station an uncontrolled reaction is in progress and explosion which will destroy the whole station will happen soon.\n\nThe station is represented by a square n ΓÇë├ùΓÇë n divided into 1ΓÇë├ùΓÇë1 blocks. Each block is either a reactor or a laboratory. There can be several reactors and exactly one of them will explode soon. The reactors can be considered impassable blocks, but one can move through laboratories. Between any two laboratories, which are in adjacent blocks, there is a corridor. Blocks are considered adjacent if they have a common edge.\n\nIn each laboratory there is some number of scientists and some number of rescue capsules. Once the scientist climbs into a capsule, he is considered to be saved. Each capsule has room for not more than one scientist.\n\nThe reactor, which is about to explode, is damaged